Technical Requirements Document (TRD)System Overview
The software continuously monitors a designated WhatsApp group for incoming
messages containing PDF documents. Upon receiving a PDF, it parses the
document, searches for a target row/amount matching specific search rules,
crops that row into an image, uploads the image to cloud storage, and
dispatches an SMS containing the extracted data and proof image URL.

Additionally, the system maintains high availability by monitoring its own
WhatsApp session health. It emits immediate alert SMS messages upon session
disconnection, authentication failure, or process downtime.

Technical Specifications1. Functional Requirements1.1 WhatsApp Client &
Session Monitoring

   - *Authentication:* Maintain a persistent Chromium/WhatsApp Web session
   using whatsapp-web.js (or Puppeteer-based equivalent) store session
   tokens locally.

   - *Lifecycle Event Listening:*

   - Detect authenticated and ready states.

      - Detect auth_failure and disconnected events.

      - *Active Health Check (Heartbeat):*

   - Periodically invoke client.getState() every 15 minutes.

      - If the state is not CONNECTED or the call times out (30s
      threshold), flag a session crash.

      - *Auto-Reconnection Attempt:*

   - Attempt up to 3 automatic re-initializations (exponential backoff:
      30s, 60s, 120s) on session loss.

      - If all retry attempts fail, emit a *Critical Session Failure Alert*=
.


1.2 Message & PDF Processing

   - *Group Filtering:* Listen exclusively to incoming messages from a
   configured TARGET_GROUP_ID. Ignore all other private/group messages.

   - *Media Identification:* Filter for attachments with MIME type
   application/pdf.

   - *Data Extraction:*

   - Render PDF pages to extract structural layout and raw text (pdfplumber
      / pypdf).

      - Locate the row containing target identifiers (e.g., regex matching
      specific invoice numbers, keywords, or balance line items).

      - Extract target text fields (e.g., entity name, total amount due,
      due date).

      - *Evidence Cropping:*

   - Convert the target PDF page into a high-resolution PNG image.

      - Crop the image bounding box around the target row with a 20px
      padding margin.

      - Upload the cropped PNG to cloud storage (AWS S3 / GCP Storage /
      Vercel Blob) with a unique filename (/evidence/YYYYMMDD_UUID.png).

      - Generate a shortened, direct access URL.


1.3 SMS Dispatch Engine

   - *Integration:* Connect to a telephony API (Twilio / Vonage) via REST
   SDK.

   - *Message Templates:*

   - *Target Data Found Alert:*
      [ALERT] PDF Data Extracted: <KEYWORD> - Amount: <AMOUNT>. Evidence:
      <EVIDENCE_URL>

      - *Session Failure Alert:*
      [CRITICAL] WhatsApp Bot Session Disconnected! Reason: <REASON>.
      Re-authentication (QR scan) required.

      - *Character Budget Optimization:* Ensure SMS body remains strictly
   under *160 characters* (1 SMS segment) to minimize delivery fees.


System Architecture & Data Flow

+-------------------+      (Incoming Message)      +-----------------------=
+
|  WhatsApp Group   | ---------------------------> |  WhatsApp Listener    =
|
+-------------------+                              | (Node.js/Puppeteer)   =
|
                                                   +-----------------------=
+
                                                               |
                                                  [Health / Exception Check=
]
                                                               |

+--------------------+--------------------+
                                          | (Session Alive)
             | (Session Dead)
                                          v
             v
                               +--------------------+
 +--------------------+
                               |  PDF Processor     |
 | Session Recovery   |
                               |  & Cropper Engine  |
 | Retry Engine       |
                               +--------------------+
 +--------------------+
                                          |
             |
                                    [Uploads Image]
       [Retry Fails]
                                          v
             v
                               +--------------------+
 +--------------------+
                               |  Cloud Storage     |
 |  Twilio SMS API    |
                               |  (AWS S3 / CDN)    |
 |  (Failure Alert)   |
                               +--------------------+
 +--------------------+
                                          |
             |
                                   [Short URL Generated]
             v
                                          |
 +--------------------+

+---------------------------> | Destination Mobile |

 +--------------------+

Component Requirements & Interface ContractsConfiguration Interface (
config.env)
Bash

# Telephony
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=3DACxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=3Dxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
TWILIO_FROM_NUMBER=3D+1234567890
ALERT_DESTINATION_NUMBER=3D+1987654321
# WhatsApp Configuration
TARGET_GROUP_ID=3D120363xxxxxxxx@g.us
SESSION_DATA_PATH=3D./.wwebjs_auth
# Cloud Storage
AWS_S3_BUCKET_NAME=3Dpdf-evidence-vault
AWS_S3_REGION=3Dus-east-1
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=3DAKIAxxxxxxxx
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=3Dxxxxxxxx
# Target Parsing Rules
PDF_TARGET_REGEX=3D(?i)(total\s*due|amount\s*payable)

Module Breakdown
*Module Name* *Language/Stack* *Responsibility*
*SessionManager* Node.js / whatsapp-web.js Manages auth, listens to
auth_failure/disconnected, executes heartbeat checks, handles
auto-reconnects.
*PdfExtractor* Python (pdfplumber + Pillow) or Node.js (pdf-lib +
canvas) Downloads
PDF bytes, locates bounding box coordinates for string matches, crops PNG
canvas, exports image stream.
*StorageService* AWS SDK (@aws-sdk/client-s3) Receives PNG buffer, uploads
to S3 with public-read permissions or presigned expiration, returns short
URL.
*SmsNotifier* Twilio SDK Handles queued message dispatch, logs delivery
status callback errors, executes fallback retries.Non-Functional
Requirements1. Reliability & Resilience

   - *Process Persistence:* Execute using a process manager (PM2 or Docker
   container restart policy unless-stopped).

   - *Session Deduplication:* Log processed PDF file hashes (MD5) to
   prevent duplicate SMS alerts if WhatsApp re-emits message events.

   - *Network Fault Tolerance:* Wrap all HTTP API calls (Twilio, AWS S3) in
   exponential backoff retry loops.


2. Error Handling & Edge Cases
*Failure Mode* *Trigger Condition* *System Action*
*WhatsApp Logout* User logs out linked device via phone app. Emits
auth_failure event =E2=86=92 Triggers immediate *Critical SMS Alert*.
*Headless Browser Crash* Memory leak or Chromium crash. Process Manager
(PM2) restarts script =E2=86=92 Health check fails recovery =E2=86=92 Sends=
 SMS.
*Unreadable PDF / Image OCR* Vector text unavailable (scanned PDF image). S=
ends
SMS: [WARNING] PDF received in <GROUP> but text layer was unreadable.
*Target String Not Found* PDF contains no match for search regex. Logs
event to audit trail; silently skips SMS (or sends optional debug log).3.
Security

   - *Data Minimization:* Delete temporary PDF files and local cropped
   images immediately after S3 upload.

   - *Credentials:* Keep API tokens, phone numbers, and cloud keys strictly
   in environment variables; never hardcode credentials.

